<title>USA: US SPR crude sale in 2002 no longer needed - Pena.</title>
<headline>US SPR crude sale in 2002 no longer needed - Pena.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on economic projections, the Clinton administration dropped a proposal to sell $1.145 billion of crude oil from the strategic petroleum reserve in 2002, Energy Secretary Federico Pena said Friday.</p>
<p>Pena said based on economic projections, the administration felt that it was no longer necessary in the balanced budget plan to sell off the crude oil.</p>
</text>
